From: jahshaka <jahshaka@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] clusterlod: an optional prune (clodConfig::simplify_prune) and a per-group simplify report

ATOM-6, 2026-10-20. meshopt_simplify's edge collapse never removes a connected
component, so a group made of many small pieces (a leaf card is two triangles,
a railing post a closed box) cannot reach half its triangles: it is terminal at
depth 0 or falls to the sloppy fallback, and the chain ends there (Bistro: 168
of 722 DAG meshes end above 128 triangles and hold 175,151 of the scene's
281,644 coarsest triangles). clodConfig::simplify_prune adds
meshopt_SimplifyPrune to the group simplification's options (default OFF:
upstream's behaviour exactly).

The report: clodGroup::simplify_flags (CLOD_SIMPLIFY_SLOPPY when the sloppy
fallback produced the group's result) and clodGroup::locked_dropped (how many
of the group's locked positions — the level's boundary, terminal and input
locks, by welded position — the result no longer uses: an edge collapse never removes one; the
sloppy fallback and a pruned component, which meshoptimizer v1.2 removes
regardless of its locks, can). The root group reports 0 for both.

Applied at configure (irisgl/CMakeLists.txt) to a copy of the vendored header
in the build tree; the vendored file itself is never edited.
---
--- a/clusterlod.h
+++ b/clusterlod.h
@@ -55,6 +55,10 @@
 	// use regularization during simplification to make triangle density more uniform, at some cost to overall triangle count; recommended for deformable objects
 	bool simplify_regularize;
 
+	// remove disconnected components of a group while simplifying it (meshopt_SimplifyPrune): an edge collapse never removes a
+	// connected component, so a group made of many small pieces (leaf cards, kit-bashed parts) cannot otherwise reach its target
+	bool simplify_prune;
+
 	// should clodCluster::bounds be computed based on the geometry of each cluster
 	bool optimize_bounds;
 
@@ -143,6 +147,17 @@
 	// 1. clodGroup::simplified for the group it's in is over error threshold
 	// 2. cluster.refined is -1 *or* clodGroup::simplified for groups[cluster.refined].simplified is at or under error threshold
 	clodBounds simplified;
+
+	// how the group's (last) simplification went: CLOD_SIMPLIFY_* bits, and how many of the group's locked vertices it lost
+	// (by welded position; an edge collapse never removes a locked vertex; the sloppy fallback and a pruned component can)
+	unsigned int simplify_flags;
+	unsigned int locked_dropped;
+};
+
+// clodGroup::simplify_flags
+enum
+{
+	CLOD_SIMPLIFY_SLOPPY = 1 << 0, // the sloppy fallback produced the result
 };
 
